1
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:06,380
Seven years later,

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,880
in 1888,

3
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:13,740
Jack the Ripper stalked
the streets of London,

4
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:18,880
murdering women in the night and holding
the entire city in his thrall. However,

5
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:22,437
he was nothing compared to
the horror that the feud

6
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:25,480
between JoJo and D would
unleash upon the world.

7
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,720
Let's go.

8
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:05,900
I will say the world
will be the only way I am

9
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:14,000
I will show the world to the world
The world will be the only way I am

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,657
I will say the word that

11
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:23,577
I am The future will be

12
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:28,000
the only way I am It's a
movement that I will burn

13
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:09,170
Interception!

14
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:10,390
Interception!

15
00:02:10,473 --> 00:02:12,725
The ball is plucked out
of the air by our hero,

16
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,560
Jonathan Joestar!

17
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:22,800
Joestar, a gentle giant
at 195 centimeters,

18
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:25,800
sprints for the trizone
with a spirited roar!

19
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:27,940
Can he win this?

20
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:30,334
The last game of his university career!

21
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,420
He's tackled from behind!

22
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:35,570
Wait!

23
00:02:35,653 --> 00:02:36,940
He's still standing tall!

24
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,140
Two more fly in!

25
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:42,020
It's three on one out there!

26
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:48,910
Incredible!

27
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:53,737
He's still making for the try line,
undaunted by the men who dog his steps!

28
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,700
What power!

29
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,078
What determination!

30
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,800
He's Hercules reborn!

31
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,200
Another tackle!

32
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:05,140
Oh, the weight's too much for him!

33
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,820
He flings it away and...

34
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:12,590
Yes!

35
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,400
There's the catch!

36
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:17,326
The ball lands safe in
the hands of Diobrando!

37
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:19,320
It's still anyone's game!

38
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:25,220
Can he make it?

39
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:27,680
He dodges one and another!

40
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:29,200
He's done it!

41
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:34,165
There's nothing left between Dio and the
try line, and still he gives it his all!

42
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,210
Yes!

43
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,220
They did it!

44
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:41,701
On the last play, they snatched
victory out of the doors of defeat!

45
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,820
What teamwork!

46
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:46,966
When Jojo and Dio work together,
there's nothing they can't do!

47
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:48,480
Hell of a pass, Jojo.

48
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:51,017
All for naught if you hadn't
run it in like you did.

49
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:54,865
Watching you drag those defenders,
I couldn't just let you down.

50
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:59,493
Having finished his studies, Dio is
set to graduate with top marks in law.

51
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,647
Jojo, meanwhile, has set the faculty
afire with his bold thesis on archaeology.

52
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:08,300
On and off the field, these
two young men are giants.

53
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:10,502
They're the pride of our school.

54
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:15,192
Jojo, I think we should tell our father
about this victory of ours at once.

55
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:24,477
It's been seven years now since my father

56
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:27,960
welcomed Dio into our
home Seven long years

57
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:32,340
I smile and treat him as
a brother But in my heart,

58
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:34,696
nothing can be further from the truth

59
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:38,560
He's nothing if not
affable And smart as a whip

60
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,920
But I just can't forgive
him for his early villainies

61
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:50,497
Dio, might you give us a quote
about your friendship with Jojo?

62
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:55,080
You seem quite close Right about
the team, all of us Come on,

63
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,791
tell us how close you are

64
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,340
Hmm, should I?

65
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:01,981
Friendship, huh?

66
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,400
The truth is,

67
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:09,737
I despise this grinning imbecile I've spent
seven years making nice to that Joestar

68
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:13,397
brat But now that I am of age I shall

69
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:17,140
bring my plans to fruition At long last,

70
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:22,540
the Joestar fortune will be mine And
devil take anyone who tries to stop me

71
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:30,380
Father, how are you feeling today?

72
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:34,820
But for this cough, much
improved over yesterday

73
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:39,720
The doctors say I should
be in the hospital Why?

74
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,020
I fear it would do you no good

75
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:45,757
Hospitals only care about profit They'd

76
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:48,605
measure you for a shroud
ere they saw you cured

77
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:53,540
Then here I shall remain The comforts
of home are curative like as not

78
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:58,440
My chest doesn't pain me so
And the swelling has gone down

79
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:03,900
I'm on the mend It was just a
cold Why has it worsened so?

80
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:06,920
I heard tell of your victory.

81
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,631
Stunning bit of teamwork.

82
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,840
Someone told you about it?

83
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,340
I got word straight away
from an old college chum.

84
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,200
Whoever he is, he's fast.

85
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:20,205
I'm glad he wasn't on our opponent's
team or we could have lost.

86
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,440
I'm proud of you, lads.

87
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:24,620
You both turned out so well.

88
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,520
Providence is too kind.

89
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:30,357
Dio, I'm so glad you've thrived.

90
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:32,937
Pursue your ambitions,
whatever they may be.

91
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:37,000
I will lend you aid in
any way I can, my son.

92
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,980
You rescued me from calamity.

93
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:42,966
Already my debt is more
than I can ever repay.

94
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,800
You do me too much honor.

95
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,420
The secret is mine alone.

96
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:07,667
I can't imagine for what purpose this
mask may have been fashioned, or by whom.

97
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:11,880
But it belonged to my mother, and
so having it near is a comfort,

98
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,760
strange as that may seem.

99
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:17,480
When I finally outwit
the sphinx of a mask,

100
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:20,544
it will be the talk of
the archaeological world.

101
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:22,460
My goodness!

102
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:31,740
Many thanks to you, Master Dio.

103
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:33,130
Hmm.

104
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:34,597
The years betray me.

105
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:37,856
Climbing the stairs is much
harder than it was before.

106
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:40,520
This letter!

107
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:43,520
Having read it, all has been made clear!

108
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:45,890
Dio!

109
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:49,900
I think he's...

110
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:57,350
Dio!

111
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,560
Wait, that's...

112
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:02,400
That's father's medicine.

113
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:07,460
He's due for his next dosage.

114
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,937
All this time, you're the one
who's been bringing it to him.

115
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:12,460
Yes, what of it?

116
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:13,600
This letter.

117
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,560
Your father sent it to mine.

118
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,078
Guess what it says.

119
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:20,580
Your lordship, sickness
has laid me right low.

120
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:23,399
It's the end of me, whatever it is.

121
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,680
My chest hurts,

122
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:30,397
my fingers are all swollen up, and I
can't breathe but for all this coughing.

123
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,833
Those are the same symptoms as father's.

124
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:33,790
Blow for blow.

125
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,882
No way is this mere coincidence.

126
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,110
Dio!

127
00:08:37,193 --> 00:08:38,920
What are you trying to say, Jojo?

128
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,673
I'm having a doctor look at this powder.

129
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:48,280
Jojo, if you think I would poison father,

130
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:52,780
then from this day forward,
you and I are friends no more.

131
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:57,760
Try as I might, I can't
look Dio in the eye.

132
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,800
It's because I lack proof.

133
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:02,335
All I have to go on are my suspicions.

134
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:06,020
Now then, if you put that
medicine back on the tray,

135
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:10,015
I'll be willing to forget
about your lapse in judgment.

136
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:15,677
Dio, there's only one way
you're going to convince me.

137
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:18,077
Swear to me that the
contents of this are safe.

138
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:19,454
Do it in Dario's name.

139
00:09:19,940 --> 00:09:22,528
Swear to me on Dario's
honor as a gentleman.

140
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:25,721
Do that and I'll never
bring up this moment again.

141
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,460
If my hunch proves true,

142
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:32,705
his father's honor is the one lie
that will catch in his throat.

143
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:33,890
Say it!

144
00:09:33,973 --> 00:09:35,371
What are you waiting for?

145
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:38,160
I... swear...

146
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:45,320
How can I swear on the honor
of a man who didn't have any?

147
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,420
He deserved to die!

148
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:49,484
How's that for the truth, Jojo?

149
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:55,980
You just gave me all
the proof I needed, Dio.

150
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,960
At hearing his name, you lashed out.

151
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:03,177
I don't know what he could have done
that moved you to such murderous rage,

152
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:05,025
but murder him you surely did!

153
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:13,760
You hurt father never again, Dio!

154
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,340
Damn your eyes.

155
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:26,560
Of course.

156
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:29,177
You've been planning to
murder him for years now.

157
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,090
I knew it.

158
00:10:30,173 --> 00:10:32,097
I knew that you were playing Foss with us.

159
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:34,060
But now your villainy is over.

160
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:39,233
Once I've learned what this is, I'm
taking it to the police straight away.

161
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:42,810
Damn it.

162
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,180
Their fortune was within my grasp.

163
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:49,260
Was it fate that Jojo
found out when he did?

164
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:50,930
No.

165
00:10:51,013 --> 00:10:52,360
No, it was that letter.

166
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:54,640
He vexes me, even now!

167
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:57,920
You're weak, just like your mother!

168
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:00,980
He drove her to an early grave.

169
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:06,860
Knowing that curse blood flows through
my veins, it's enough to drive me mad!

170
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:15,600
Ser Joestar lives, for now.

171
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:26,425
I'll be back from London
in a few days, Father.

172
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:31,806
Till then, accept medicine only from the
hands of these doctors and no one else.

173
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:36,300
Master Jojo said he doesn't
want me to bring it up? Yes.

174
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:39,300
We will do as Jojo has instructed us.

175
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:45,720
His reasons are a mystery to me,
but I trust the boy with my life.

176
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:48,039
Thank you, Father.

177
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:51,815
However, his illness is getting worse.

178
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:56,860
If it is a poison, he
may need an antidote.

179
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:04,201
Whatever you may learn in
London about the poison,

180
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:07,324
I'll see you take the
truth of it to your grave.

181
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:11,020
Your death will be the perfect crime.

182
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:15,737
Seven years ago, this
mask reacted to my blood.

183
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:20,120
The spikes hidden within will
make short work of Jojo's brain.

184
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:25,500
His injuries will be so unique, there'll
be nothing at all to tie it back to me.

185
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:31,020
Jojo, your curiosity will
lead to your destruction.

186
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:40,640
The university couldn't identify
this so-called medicine,

187
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:44,804
though they did speculate that it
was a compound from the Orient.

188
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:47,550
Therefore...

189
00:12:47,633 --> 00:12:50,800
Young Master, that stretch
of road there is Ogre Street,

190
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:53,617
the most dangerous
alleyway in all of London.

191
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:54,640
Yes, I know.

192
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:58,437
But this is the one place I will
be able to find what I came for.

193
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,520
You're more than welcome to leave.

194
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:03,640
Dio grew up in London.

195
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:07,432
Where else in England could
he have acquired such a toxin?

196
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:11,560
I shall have my evidence
and Father's Antidote.

197
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,820
Another dead end.

198
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:25,180
That cat, it was eating a puppy.

199
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:31,800
You do the honors, Tattoo. Right!

200
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,637
Use that shiv of yours to slice him open.

201
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,480
I want his guts for garters.

202
00:13:37,140 --> 00:13:39,820
Ogre street, it is aptly named.

203
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:47,700
Check out this idiot!

204
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,136
He grabbed my blade!

205
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:51,772
In all my days, I've never seen the like!

206
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:53,960
Stuck, ain't ya?

207
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:56,097
One quick yank of the
knife and I'll be picking

208
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:58,557
your fingers out of the
snow for a fortnight.

209
00:13:58,640 --> 00:13:59,470
Try it, then.

210
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,020
The moment you pull,

211
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:05,037
my foot will kick out at your groin
with all the force of a sledgehammer.

212
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,377
I'm willing to see our
transaction through.

213
00:14:07,460 --> 00:14:08,290
Are you, Syrah?

214
00:14:08,373 --> 00:14:11,937
I'm fighting to protect my family
from those who wish it harm.

215
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:15,138
I doubt very much that your
resolve is equal to mine.

216
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:20,636
That's quite enough.

217
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:25,480
Now tell me, one of you, where can I
find an Asian apothecary? Tough talk.

218
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:28,956
If you're looking to lose
body parts, do stick around.

219
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,330
Observe.

220
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:41,056
I'll mince you right finally,
with the tip of the hat.

221
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:45,000
And now we dance.

222
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:49,620
I have to find that
apothecary, no matter the cost.

223
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:52,937
Don't tell me this here's
your first proper dust-up.

224
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:56,491
If you mean to block like that,
it'll be your last one too.

225
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:02,150
Ha-ha!

226
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:04,857
Cut you straight to the bone, looks like.

227
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:07,777
Granted, I didn't think you'd
hooved the shiv at me like that,

228
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:09,860
but my chapeau still hit its mark.

229
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:18,680
Now I know why he weren't
defending himself better.

230
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,560
Fingers, hands, legs.

231
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:23,036
He don't care one whit what he loses.

232
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:26,380
It's as if his resolve runs
deeper than pain or fear.

233
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:28,757
I took the lad for an easy mark.

234
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,800
I guess I've been right
disabused of that notion.

235
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,110
What?

236
00:15:43,193 --> 00:15:44,960
JoJo went to Ogre Street on his own?

237
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,760
I told him it was perilous.

238
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,514
Keep this to yourself.

239
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,507
Sir Joestar is still unwell.

240
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:52,830
Yes, sir.

241
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:55,985
I guess I won't need to
use the mask after all.

242
00:15:57,420 --> 00:15:59,400
There, alone, his fate is sealed.

243
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:04,080
That's enough, lads.

244
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:08,740
I won't let a single one of you lay
a finger on that gentleman there.

245
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:10,960
But why?

246
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,317
Tell me something.

247
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:15,988
Strong as a bull you
are, it's plain to see.

248
00:16:16,420 --> 00:16:19,017
You could have stove my head
in with that foot of yours,

249
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:21,218
but you went easy on me, didn't you?

250
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:27,997
I came here for the sake of
my father You have a family

251
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:31,315
People who expect you to
return from this dark business

252
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:34,560
It is not my place to cause them grief

253
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:36,960
He means it, don't he?

254
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:40,380
How this fella survived so long Wait

255
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:45,760
He spared my mate's lives
just like he did mine

256
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:49,500
I like the cut of his jib Sure he's naive,

257
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:52,677
but he's a gentleman through
and through this one.

258
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:55,407
I want to know the name
of him who spared me.

259
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,480
Jonathan Joestar.

260
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:01,537
Well, pleased to make your acquaintance.

261
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:04,917
If it's Asian concoctions you're
looking for, mind your back.

262
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,360
The druggist is one sly customer.

263
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:13,160
So Joestar, Jojo's been gone three days.

264
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,972
Whatever his errand, he'll accomplish it.

265
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:18,197
Where have the years gone, I wonder?

266
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:19,960
He's grown into a fine man.

267
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:24,340
I cannot help but wonder if I was
too hard on the boy growing up.

268
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:39,080
I'm sure Jojo's laying
dead in some alley by now.

269
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:41,800
Did he find the apothecary?

270
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:45,157
Look at me, swilling it down.

271
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:50,440
Nothing but a drunken fool, just
like my bastard father, damn it!

272
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:57,400
Watch yourself, or have you no
respect for your elders, boy?

273
00:17:58,360 --> 00:18:01,280
Look at the baby, tolling
round past bedtime,

274
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:04,422
sucking on a bottle like
it was his mother's tea.

275
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:09,056
Look at the man when he's talking,
didn't your old man teach you right?

276
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:15,465
Oh my god, just for that, I'm
gonna take your face clean off ya!

277
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:20,400
Oh, your threat has me quaking
in my boots, you old guttersnipe.

278
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:23,246
How will I escape this
moment of mortal peril?

279
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:27,400
How about we use this?

280
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:32,040
It's meant for Jojo, but
you'll make a fine guinea pig.

281
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,580
Just die already!

282
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:38,140
Yeah, yeah, let's see what you can do

283
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:49,900
That light

284
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:05,800
All of that spectacle, for nothing.

285
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:08,090
Useless.

286
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:10,180
That was boring.

287
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,760
I expected more from you, Mask.

288
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:29,970
Impossible.

289
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:35,400
He's alive!

290
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:40,160
That face!

291
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:41,380
Those teeth!

292
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:43,950
No!

293
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:55,960
What incredible strength!

294
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:09,780
Even now he advances, but his
hand, does the pain mean nothing?

295
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:13,600
He shattered my shoulder
with but a glancing blow.

296
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:18,560
The river, I must jump in.

297
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:26,240
It's odd.

298
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:31,217
I was drinking through the night, but
suddenly I got such a brutal thirst.

299
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:32,560
My blood!

300
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:34,100
It's draining it!

301
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:38,240
What the...

302
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:41,760
So this is the secret of the mask.

303
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,640
I'm dying.

304
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:49,110
No!

305
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,480
I had such plans!

306
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:53,998
Must my last sight on Earth
be this damnable sunrise?

307
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:14,780
The sun destroyed him.

308
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:37,717
What's the meaning of this?

309
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,460
Why is it so bloody dark?

310
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:44,290
Jojo.

311
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:46,480
You're a poisoner, Dio Brando.

312
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:49,626
I have all the proof I
require, and then some.

313
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:14,037
I'll be the roundabout The words will make

314
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:19,740
you out and out I'll
spend the day your way

315
00:22:21,380 --> 00:22:25,840
Call it morning driving through
the sun And in and out the valley

316
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:40,537
The music dance and sing They make the

317
00:22:40,620 --> 00:22:47,360
children really ring I
spend the day your way

318
00:22:48,380 --> 00:22:53,140
Cold in morning driving through
the sun And in and out the valley

319
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:57,720
Then out around the lake

320
00:22:58,740 --> 00:23:02,820
Now let's come out of the
sky And they'll stand there

321
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:09,640
When my lover will be
there And we'll see you

322
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:15,960
Ten true summers We'll
be there Laughing too

323
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:24,380
Twenty-four and five My lover
will see I'll be there with you

324
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:32,940
Jojo, I've been a devil,
but grant me this one wish.

325
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:35,137
This fellow reeks of brimstone and blood!

326
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:38,840
You see, I am about to
become so much more! Dio!
